// emit -- the shape of the generated tree.
//
// The layout is the interesting decision, and it is forced by two rules that the
// generated source obeys just as the hand-written source does: at most 3 functions
// in a file, and at most 3 entries in a directory. So the chunk functions come in
// groups of three, one group per file, and the files spill down a chain:
//
//     data/d0.id        chunks 0 1 2      (data_src, data_s1, data_s2)
//     data/n/d1.id      chunks 3 4 5      (data_s3 .. data_s5)
//     data/n/n/d2.id    chunks 6 7 8
//
// Every directory in that chain then holds exactly two entries -- one .id file and
// one subdirectory -- so it can grow without limit. The project root holds main.id
// and data/, which is two, leaving room for a game's own hand-written id/ hooks to
// be imported rather than copied.

// Two actions and a return clause, and the return clause is where the engine is
// entered. idem_boot(string[] chunks, int argc, string[] argv) -> int joins the
// chunks, lexes them, and gives back the process exit code.
// A game with its own `id/` is a game written the right way round -- it owns its
// state and rules and uses the document for layout -- so it enters through
// idem_app. One without is a document the engine interprets, which is the model
// docs/IDML.md withdraws; it enters through idem_boot until it is converted.
//
// The shell tells us which, because the shell is what can see a directory.
pack_entry() {
  string s = "idem_boot";
  if ((import pack_mode)[0] = "app") { s = "idem_app"; }
} return string s;

pack_boot2() {
  print("  string[] chunks = []");
  print("  data_src(chunks)");
  pack_boot3();
} return void;

// idem_app takes its game's six functions as arguments (docs/TODO.md 14) --
// idem_boot does not, so only "app" mode's call names them, by the fixed names
// a game written the right way round defines (app.id).
pack_boot3() {
  string tail = "";
  if ((import pack_mode)[0] = "app") { tail = ", g_init, g_stage, g_step, g_draw, g_ref, g_act"; }
  string pack_entry_v = pack_entry();
  print("} return int " + pack_entry_v + "(chunks, argc, argv" + tail + ");");
} return void;

// One generated file per turn of this loop. The `|| k = 0` is not a special case
// for its own sake: a game with no idml at all must still produce a data_src for
// main.id to call, or the packed project would not link.
// `charat(src, p) >= 0` and not `p < len(src)`: len is a strlen on every
// evaluation, so testing it per turn of a loop over the whole source is
// quadratic. charat remembers the last string's length and answers -1 past the
// end, which is the same question asked once (engine/core/util/str.id).
